  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Exactly as Title states, using the new launch option to try and mitigate the issue with AMD GPU's simply just DOES NOT work properly, and needs to be further Tested and tweaked. \n\nthe new launch option works as intended, BUT has a MAJOR draw back for viewing content. Any environment recorded in darker environments, such as night scenes, underwater, caves, shadows, ETC. are unable to be seen in the proper way that it was intended to. This also includes scenes that are in broad daylight, dimming the brightness of the playback media to near impossible recognition of what's going on in the playback. \n\nmy in game Display brightness  settings are the same as they always have been while watching media playback and after the beta update, its almost pitch dark.\n\ndriver version 23.3.2, and up to date with other hardware\n\nTested with-RX6900XT",
